What to Pack in a Period Emergency Kit

A period emergency kit can be extremely useful when you are away from home. Whether you are going to school, college, work, travelling, or spending a day outside, a small kit can help you handle unexpected menstrual bleeding with confidence.

The most important item is, of course, sanitary pads. Carry at least a few spare pads rather than only one. Your period may arrive unexpectedly or your flow may be heavier than expected.

If your menstrual flow changes throughout your period, consider carrying different pad sizes. A regular pad may be suitable for lighter bleeding, while a longer or more absorbent pad can be useful for heavier flow.

